<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>the only thing i have is myself</title>
  <meta name="author" content="Muskan Hashim" />
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: monospace;
      background: #fff;
      color: #111;
      max-width: 640px;
      margin: 80px auto;
      padding: 0 24px;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      font-weight: normal;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }
    .date {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: #999;
      margin-bottom: 48px;
      display: block;
    }
    p {
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      margin-bottom: 1.4em;
    }
    .back {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 64px;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: #999;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .back:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>the only thing i have is myself</h1>

  <p>
    I was in grade 10 when one of the guys who liked me punched a glass window at school because someone else asked me out.
  </p>

  <p>
    Then there were the love letters etched out in blood in grade 12.
  </p>

  <p>
    At 19, the 38 year old man who liked me wrote a book about me, and then left me in the country he flew me out to (because I asked).
  </p>

  <p>
    Love is ugly, and it doesn’t exist.
  </p>

  <p>
    My father keeps apologizing for abandoning me, thinking any amount of money would bring me my childhood back, or make me somehow act my age now.
  </p>

  <p>
    Unfortunately, I’m wiser than that. It must be nice to lose yourself in love but I don’t have the heart to lose anymore than I have. The only thing I have is myself.
  </p>

  <a class="back" href="index.html">← all posts</a>

</body>
</html>
